ore to fend for himself against these  red-eyed creatures  and makes his way to tatooine where we  reunite with peli motto  she recalls how he hates droids droids  killed his parents after all but he's  had a change of heart  well so he likes droids now a result of  how a droid like ig-11  sacrificed himself at the end of season  one pelly tells mando that moss pelgo  was wiped out by bandits and can barely  be found on any maps we even get a nice  reintroduction to  r5d4 the droid the jawas tried to sell  to luke in a new hope she also makes  reference to a city on tatooine called  moss espa which you might remember as  the site of the pod races in the phantom  menace  mando grabs a speeder and heads off to  this mysterious mining town of moss  pelgo arriving like he's a gunslinger or  samurai in a kurosawa movie except a  horse has been substituted for a speeder  at the local cantina he meets the  proprietor from the weekway species  another race found in return of the jedi  there he meets the town's marshal which  also happens to be the title of the  episode he's a man by the name of cobb  vanth played by timothy oliphant and  he's wearing boba fett's armor the last  we saw boba fett he was thrown into the  sarlacc pit in return of the jedi so  this armor basically confirms he somehow  made it out  and we'll get to that reveal later in  the episode he tells mando he got it off  some jawas in exchange for a chem tono  of silicax crystals  something he stole from the minders  after escaping their attack on the town  after the fall of the empire if you want  to learn a little bit more about what a  camp tono is  check out my season 1 episode 1 of  breakdown this isn't the first time  cobb vanth has been seen in the star  wars universe chuck wendig's star wars  canon novel  aftermath features him arguing over a  set of mandalorian armor and includes  further backstory involving how he  fights against crime syndicates  disguising themselves as  mining companies after 