  these things  eat sarlacc the tuscans have been  feeding the crate for years in an  attempt to keep it sleeping and stopping  it from plaguing their villages  if they're gonna get this thing out  they're gonna need more people  and that's where the villagers of moss  pelgo come in the crate dragon has been  a  nuisance for the town eating their  animals and disrupting their mining  halls  and it could be any day that it totally  swallows the town whole so they decide  to join forces with the tuscans  providing much needed explosives to take  it down you may also have noticed that  during the final dragon sequence the  aspect ratio changes to full screen i'm  not 100 certain of the specs but it  probably meant this  action sequence was shot in imax and  what better way to welcome jon favreau  his first directing gig on the show  by giving him and us this awesome treat  the tuscans say that dragon's only weak  spot is its belly so if they can lure it  out on top of the explosives maybe they  stand a chance at killing it they do  everything they can to get its attention  but their barrage of ballista  blasters and grenades isn't enough the  explosives go off but it only infuriates  the dragon further  vomiting out its carosa bile at its  attackers  its care pace is just too strong even  for the explosives so mando takes  matters into his own hands by  luring the dragon next to a bantha  loaded with dynamite even knocks cobb's  jetpack to make him get out of the way  even telling cobb beforehand to take  care of the child he's willing to  sacrifice himself for this the dragon  completely swallows both mando and the  bantha but a few moments later spits  mando out after he uses his ammon phase  pulse blaster  which has an electrocution feature we  saw him use this briefly in season 1  against the trandoshan bounty hunters  mando hits the detonator the dragon  explodes and 10 year old me watching  tremors for the first time  jumps for joy you sucker  with the dragon defeated cobb hands over  the armor and tells mando he hopes their  paths cross again so this might not be  the last time we see him he also says to  tell his fellow mandalorians that he  wasn't the one to break that armor that  was likely caused by the sarlacc however  we do not know what happened between  boba fett getting thrown into the pit  and how it eventually ended up with the  jawas perhaps that will be revealed  with the introduction of boba fett  himself the end of the episode sees  actor tamura morrison who played  jango fett in the prequels reveal  himself as boba fett remember that jango  was allowed to keep one of his clone  sons to raise on his own this was boba  fett who would grow up to look  exactly like jango since he's a clone it  raises many  questions like why he's been in hiding  and how or why he let his armor go  he's got a couple scars on his face so  he's been through a lot  he's also been following mando and his  adventures on tatooine the end of  episode 5 sees a  tattered robe figure hover over the  corpse of fenik shan  a tattered robe which boba also wears at  the end of this episode for those of you  who've seen my season 1 episode 5  breakdown  you'll remember that the same boot spur  sound effect used for that robed  character is the same exact sound effect  used when boba fett walks in empire  strikes back check out the 9 minute and  30 second marker in that video if you  want to hear it for yourself  i'll leave a link in the description a  particular note in this episode is the  absence of moff gideon who we saw  survive his crash and emerge from his  ship holding a dark saber  unfortunately we're gonna have to wait a  bit longer to have him back and i  wouldn't be surprised if part of next  episode continues on tatooine  especially knowing mando is likely on a  crash course with boba fett  whether or not he's friend or foe  remains to be seen  thanks for watching everyone every  little like subscribe and share helps so  much so  make sure to do that for more bad takes  you can follow me on twitter and  instagram  at thinkstoryyt and until next time  remember  i have spoken

